[326.109156, "o", "\u001b[4mpodman\u001b[24m(1)                                                 General Commands Manual                                                 \u001b[4mpodman\u001b[24m(1)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mNAME\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n     podman - Simple management tool for pods, containers and images\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mSYNOPSIS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n     \u001b[1mpodman \u001b[22m[\u001b[4moptions\u001b[24m] \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mDESCRIPTION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n     Podman  (Pod  Manager) is a fully featured container engine that is a simple daemonless tool.  Podman provides a Docker-CLI comparable\u001b[m\r\n     command line that eases the transition from other container engines and allows the management of pods, containers and images.   Simply\u001b[m\r\n     put: \u001b[1malias docker=podman\u001b[22m.  Most Podman commands can be run as a regular user, without requiring additional privileges.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n     Podman  uses  Buildah(1)  internally to create container images. Both tools share image (not container) storage, hence each can use or\u001b[m\r\n     manipulate images (but not containers) created by the other.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n     Default settings for flags are defined in \u001b[1mcontainers.conf\u001b[22m. Most settings for Remote connections use the server's containers.conf,  ex‐\u001b[m\r\n     cept when documented in man pages.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n     To manage containers, pods, volumes, networks, and images declaratively via systemd, use quadlet files. See \u001b[1mpodman-quadlet\u001b[22m(1) and \u001b[1mpod‐\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n     \u001b[1mman-systemd.unit\u001b[22m(5).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n     \u001b[1mpodman [GLOBAL OPTIONS]\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mGLOBAL OPTIONS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n   \u001b[1m--cdi-spec-dir=\u001b[4mpath\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n     The CDI spec directory path (may be set multiple times). Default path is \u001b[1m/etc/cdi\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n   \u001b[1m--cgroup-manager=\u001b[4mmanager\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n     The CGroup manager to use for container cgroups. Supported values are \u001b[1mcgroupfs \u001b[22mor \u001b[1msystemd\u001b[22m. Default is \u001b[4msystemd\u001b[24m unless overridden in the\u001b[m\r\n     containers.conf file.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n     Note:  Setting  this flag can cause certain commands to break when called on containers previously created by the other CGroup manager\u001b[m\r\n     type.  Note: CGroup manager is not supported in rootless mode when using CGroups Version V1.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n   \u001b[1m--config\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n     Location of config file. Mainly for docker compatibility, only the authentication parts of the config are supported.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 1 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[328.476973, "o", "\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1m--conmon\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 2 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[328.977282, "o", "\r\u001b[K     Path of the conmon binary (Default path is configured in \u001b[1mcontainers.conf\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 3 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.008118, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 4 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.0372, "o", "\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1m--connection, -c\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 5 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.066965, "o", "\r\u001b[K     Connection to use for remote podman, including Mac and Windows (excluding WSL2) machines, (Default connection is  configured  in  \u001b[1mcon‐\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 6 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.097122, "o", "\r\u001b[K     \u001b[1mtainers.conf\u001b[22m) Setting this option switches the \u001b[1m--remote \u001b[22moption to true.  Remote connections use local containers.conf for default.\u001b[m"]
[329.097154, "o", "\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 7 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.128256, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 8 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.158381, "o", "\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1m--events-backend=\u001b[4mtype\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 9 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.189157, "o", "\r\u001b[K     Backend  to  use  for storing events. Allowed values are \u001b[1mfile\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mjournald\u001b[22m, and \u001b[1mnone\u001b[22m. When \u001b[4mfile\u001b[24m is specified, the events are stored under\u001b[m"]
[329.189193, "o", "\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 10 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.219756, "o", "\r\u001b[K     \u001b[1m<tmpdir>/events/events.log \u001b[22m(see \u001b[1m--tmpdir \u001b[22mbelow).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 11 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.250401, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 12 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.280871, "o", "\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1m--help, -h\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 13 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.311045, "o", "\r\u001b[K     Print usage statement\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 14 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.341654, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 15 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.372422, "o", "\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1m--hooks-dir=\u001b[4mpath\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 16 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.403266, "o", "\r\u001b[K     Each \u001b[1m*.json \u001b[22mfile in the path configures a hook for Podman containers.  For more details on the syntax of the JSON files and the seman‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 17 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.433534, "o", "\r\u001b[K     tics of hook injection, see \u001b[1moci-hooks(5)\u001b[22m.  Podman and libpod currently support both the 1.0.0 and 0.1.0  hook  schemas,  although  the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 18 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.463891, "o", "\r\u001b[K     0.1.0 schema is deprecated.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 19 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.494928, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 20 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.525383, "o", "\r\u001b[K     This option may be set multiple times; paths from later options have higher precedence (\u001b[1moci-hooks(5) \u001b[22mdiscusses directory precedence).\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 21 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.555643, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 22 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.586785, "o", "\r\u001b[K     For the annotation conditions, libpod uses any annotations set in the generated OCI configuration.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 23 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.617358, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 24 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.647812, "o", "\r\u001b[K     For  the  bind-mount  conditions, only mounts explicitly requested by the caller via \u001b[1m--volume \u001b[22mare considered.  Bind mounts that libpod\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 25 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.677927, "o", "\r\u001b[K     inserts by default (e.g. \u001b[1m/dev/shm\u001b[22m) are not considered.\u001b[m\r\n"]
[329.677959, "o", "\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 26 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.708174, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 27 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.739219, "o", "\r\u001b[K     If \u001b[1m--hooks-dir \u001b[22mis unset for root callers, Podman and libpod currently default to \u001b[1m/usr/share/containers/oci/hooks.d  \u001b[22mand  \u001b[1m/etc/contain‐\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 28 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.770315, "o", "\r\u001b[K     \u001b[1mers/oci/hooks.d \u001b[22min order of increasing precedence.  Using these defaults is deprecated. Migrate to explicitly setting \u001b[1m--hooks-dir\u001b[22m.\u001b[m"]
[329.770354, "o", "\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 29 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.80069, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 30 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.831774, "o", "\r\u001b[K     Podman  and  libpod currently support an additional \u001b[1mprecreate \u001b[22mstate which is called before the runtime's \u001b[1mcreate \u001b[22moperation.  Unlike the\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 31 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.862866, "o", "\r\u001b[K     other stages, which receive the container state on their standard input, \u001b[1mprecreate \u001b[22mhooks receive the proposed runtime configuration on\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 32 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.892861, "o", "\r\u001b[K     their standard input.  They may alter that configuration as they see fit, and write the altered form to their standard output.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 33 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.923147, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 34 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.954248, "o", "\r\u001b[K     \u001b[1mWARNING\u001b[22m: the \u001b[1mprecreate \u001b[22mhook allows powerful changes to occur, such as adding additional mounts to  the  runtime  configuration.   That\u001b[m"]
[329.954273, "o", "\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 35 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[329.984464, "o", "\r\u001b[K     power  also  makes  it easy to break things.  Before reporting libpod errors, try running a container with \u001b[1mprecreate \u001b[22mhooks disabled to\u001b[m"]
[329.984487, "o", "\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 36 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.015411, "o", "\r\u001b[K     see if the problem is due to one of the hooks.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 37 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.045472, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 38 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.076427, "o", "\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1m--identity=\u001b[4mpath\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 39 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.10741, "o", "\r\u001b[K     Path to ssh identity file. If the identity file has been encrypted, podman prompts the user for the passphrase.  If no  identity  file\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 40 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.137921, "o", "\r\u001b[K     is  provided  and  no user is given, podman defaults to the user running the podman command.  Podman prompts for the login password on\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 41 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.168406, "o", "\r\u001b[K     the remote server.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 42 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.199052, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 43 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.229693, "o", "\r\u001b[K     Identity value resolution precedence:\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 44 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.260439, "o", "\r\u001b[K      - command line value\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 45 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.290505, "o", "\r\u001b[K      - environment variable \u001b[1mCONTAINER_SSHKEY\u001b[22m, if \u001b[1mCONTAINER_HOST \u001b[22mis found\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 46 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.3216, "o", "\r\u001b[K      - \u001b[1mcontainers.conf \u001b[22mRemote connections use local containers.conf for default.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 47 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.351961, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 48 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.382258, "o", "\r\u001b[K   \u001b[1m--imagestore=\u001b[4mpath\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 49 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.41288, "o", "\r\u001b[K     Path of the imagestore where images are stored.  By default, the storage library stores all the images in the graphroot but if an  im‐\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 50 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.442985, "o", "\r\u001b[K     agestore  is provided, then the storage library will store newly pulled images in the provided imagestore and keep using the graphroot\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 51 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.474043, "o", "\r\u001b[K     for everything else. If the user is using the overlay driver, then the images which were already part of the graphroot will  still  be\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 52 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.504522, "o", "\r\u001b[K     accessible.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 53 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[330.534589, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page podman(1) line 54 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
